# Bundled gems. `.bundle/config` pins BUNDLE_PATH to vendor/bundle, so a local
# `bundle install` recreates this tree in place and any `git add -A` would put
# ~3,200 files and 56 MB of native binaries (sass.snapshot, dart, *.so, *.gem
# caches) back into history. It is also dead weight: the committed tree is Ruby
# 3.0.0 while CI builds on Ruby 3.2, so it cannot serve as an offline fallback.
vendor/
.bundle/

# Unpublished drafts. Jekyll never builds `_drafts/`, but git has no notion of
# "private": anything tracked here is in every clone, is indexed by GitHub code
# search, and can be archived by third parties. Keep personal and
# pre-publication material in ~/Workspace/Blog/ref/ instead, which is not a
# public repository. See docs/review-2026-10-01.md F4.
_drafts/
